# Simple code only

- Keep every change as simple as possible.
- Prefer the smallest straight-line fix over abstractions, helpers, or extra files.
- Do not add comments, JSDoc, or explanatory notes in code.
- Do not add TODOs, section banners, or narrating comments.
- Avoid drive-by refactors, unused exports, and speculative flexibility.
- Match existing patterns; change only what the task requires.
- If two approaches work, choose the shorter one.
- Must follow our design system (`design.md` + Tailgrids primitives).

```tsx
// BAD — comments + extra indirection
/** Fetches project cost summary */
function getCost(id: string) {
  // compute from linked docs
  return compute(id);
}

// GOOD — direct
function getCost(id: string) {
  return compute(id);
}
```
